    "needsReview": false,
    "note": "Status is resident and all twelve months are listed. Newman calls it a fairly common resident. The female’s blue throat patch is the only sex difference stored. The immature face is yellow in Newman; an earlier buff value was corrected to that. Chick down beyond the yellow pouch is not described. The call is grade A from Kruger, near Skukuza. The filename says Hornbill rather than the full species name. The population figures were left unchanged."
